tentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the matrix of Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen (1993). A directed graph’s edge is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"column with one source and one target, which gives the oriented incidence matrix of spectral"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L). The matrix conforms to "},{"code":"DirectedHypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged. It is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Two bit planes","anchor":"Two-bit-planes","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sources and the targets are each stored as an ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a vertex can be on both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sides of a column. Its entry is then target − source = 0, with both bits kept.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"sources(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"targets(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the stars and equality read the planes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so nothing is lost. A directed self-loop is such a column. ","type":"text"},{"code":"reversed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" swaps the planes, negating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every entry, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"transposed()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" transposes each plane to give the dual. Both are O(1).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage is 4·n·m\/8 bytes, so the matrix suits dense or small incidence. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sparse representation. Equality compares both planes cell for cell, with equal shape, so column"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order counts."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/Se","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SE","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SH","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule"]]},"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/init(_:)-6qyfl":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-6qyfl","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/init(_:)-6qyfl","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphPro